{
  "_comment": [
    "What each JSON-encoded Sparkplug metric reads as, for the two services that decode one.",
    "",
    "  ingestion/ingestion.py   parse_sparkplug_payload()  -- what the historian stores",
    "  i3x/i3x_service.py       decode_metrics()           -- what the i3X server serves",
    "",
    "Both read a JSON metric through json_metric_value(), mirrored in each file. Each suite asserts",
    "every case below through its own parser: ingestion/test_json_payload.py and",
    "i3x/test_i3x_service.py. `reads` is the Sparkplug value, an integer read through its datatype;",
    "null means the metric carries no value. `dropped` means that metric is refused and the rest of",
    "its payload is kept. Names are unique, because i3X keys what it serves by metric name."
  ],
